OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sun 9 Aug to Tue 18 Aug
OL,6,FRain or showers clearing on Sunday,
OL,7,Fwith high pressure bringing more
OL,8,Fsettled weather for most on Monday.
OL,9,FHigh pressure will remain prevalent
OL,10,Facross the UK for a time, but low
OL,11,Fpressure in the Atlantic may bring
OL,12,Ffurther wet weather to northwestern
OL,13,Fparts. Further into August, high
OL,14,Fpressure may become more dominant
OL,15,Ftowards the north or northwest of the
OL,16,FUK, with lower pressure to the south
OL,17,For east. This means there is a greater
OL,18,Fchance of frontal systems or thundery
OL,19,Finterludes to affect southern and
OL,20,Feastern areas in comparison to recent
OL,21,Fweeks, though rainfall amounts could
OL,22,Fbe quite variable with some areas
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fstill seeing relatively little. For
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Fthe most part, temperatures look to
OL,25,Fremain above average, especially in
OL,26,Fthe south, and perhaps turning very
